{title: 151 - Jesus Walked This Lonesome Valley}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #151 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 151}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Jesus walked this lonesome valley;
He had to walk it by Himself.
O nobody else could walk it for Him.
He had to walk it by Himself.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I must go and stand my trial.
I have to stand it by myself.
O nobody else could stand it for me.
I have to stand it by myself.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Jesus walked this lonesome valley;
He had to walk it by Himself.
O nobody else could walk it for Him.
He had to walk it by Himself.
{end_of_verse}
